# Terminal rules (Ink 8)

- Everything renders inside the alternate screen at exactly `useScreen()` width and height. Never print with
  `console.log` while Ink is mounted; surface messages as a notice in state.
- Never assume a width: truncate (`wrap="truncate"`), pad, or measure with `lineLen`. Every row must fit; a
  layout is correct at 80 columns and at 200.
- Colours and glyphs come from `shared/lib/theme.ts`. No hard-coded colours in components.
- **Keys are case-insensitive.** Lower-case the input once and bind lower-case letters only; no action may
  need Shift. Arrows work wherever `j`/`k` do. Every bound key appears in the footer or the help view, and
  both stay in sync with the handler (a key that exists only in code is a bug).
- Anything that can take longer than ~100 ms (an agent, git, the filesystem) runs in the background with a
  visible spinner. The UI never blocks, and never waits on the AI to toggle a checkbox.
- Destructive actions (delete a provider, apply fixes) say what will happen and ask once; the default
  answer is the safe one.
- Test with ink-testing-library: wait for text, never for time; a key pressed before its listener attached is
  lost, so wait for the screen that owns the key first.
